  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_fit.rs`: a new step `relax` runs after the split of #2600, on each face that the split changed. It flips an inside edge when the two angles opposite to it sum to more than a half turn (Lawson's edge flip, measured in space).\n- A flip is made only when the two new facets keep their winding in the parameter plane, and the new edge passes the chord-height limit of the split. No point moves. No boundary edge changes. The facet count does not change.\n- `crates/app/tests/tilted_gouge.rs`: one new test for the normals of the bar's wall facets.\n- `docs/decisions/2713-step-cap-facets.md`: the decision and the dropped options.\n- `crates/kernel/tests/step_agreement.rs`: the missing triage row for `bar_cross_holes.step` and its named pin.\n\nThe kernel refuses this fixture with `solidcore refuses: #655 at read: pcurves failed on`. The mesh reports `no exact solid to judge against`. The row records a named refusal, not import agreement.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe join law (#2215) was not the cause. The cause is the STEP importer.\n\nThe split of #2600 measures facet edges only. On the wall of `bar_cross_holes.step` it left flat \"cap\" facets: three points on the cylinder, with the apex over the middle of the long edge. Each edge of such a facet is within the limit. The normal of the facet is not: it stood up to 65.5 degrees off the radius.\n\nThe feature graph uses a crease angle of 40 degrees. It read the edges of the cap facets as creases on the smooth wall, and some cap facets as faces of their own. These false edges were the 116 split pieces of the test.\n\n## Readings (`bar_cross_holes.step`)\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| wall facets | 131 834 | 131 834 |\n| wall facets with a normal more than 25 degrees off the radius | 2 147 | 0 |\n| worst wall normal | 65.5 degrees | 6.5 degrees |\n| pickable edges | 3 701 | 642 |\n| split pieces | 116 | 0 |\n| import time of the normals test (debug build) | 2.6 s | 5.5 s |\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `feature_edge_g1_join`: `no_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture`. This is the test of the issue. It was red on a clean `upstream/main` 75e74a9cb: `bar_cross_holes.step: 3701 pickable edges, 39259 chains, 116 split pieces`.\n- `tilted_gouge`: `the_step_bars_wall_facet_normals_follow_the_cylinder` (new). It pins the cause in the importer.\n- `step_agreement`: `step_bar_cross_holes` pins the fixture triage. `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` pins coverage of every STEP fixture. Both tests pass.\n\nMutation: with `step_fit.rs` of `upstream/main`, the two pins are red (116 split pieces; 2 147 facets, worst 65.5 degrees). With the fix, the two pins are green.\n\nKernel row mutation: removing the `bar_cross_holes.step` row makes `step_bar_cross_holes` and `step_files_agree_or_refuse_by_name` red. Restoring the row makes the suite green.\n\nThe review fix also passes the explicit suites: `camcraft-kernel --test step_agreement` (20 passed) and `camcraft-app --test feature_edge_g1_join` (5 passed).\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 23 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-kernel --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- By hand, because the quick gate did not select them: `feature_edge_g1_join` (5 passed), `golden_cl` (33 passed), `regression_models` (2 passed), `feature` (18 passed), `feature_pick` (7 passed).\n- The pins of #2600 stay green: `a_tilted_slot_into_the_step_bar_is_refused`, `the_step_bars_wall_facets_lie_on_the_cylinder`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI by hand. The pick on the bar was not looked at in the app.\n- The ui suites and the release lanes.\n- A release build. The import times are from a debug build.\n- Cone, sphere and torus faces. The fixture has cylinder faces only. The flip uses the same parameters and the same limit for each kind.\n- A cap facet whose long edge is on the boundary of the face. It cannot be flipped and stays. The fixture has none over the limit of the test.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes `step_fit.rs` or `tilted_gouge.rs`.\n\nChangelog: A STEP bar or tube with a cross hole no longer shows false edges on its smooth wall; the facets of a refined curved face now follow the surface normal.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2713\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
